routing.adsapi-ads-account-diagnostics:
# AGENTS

When a conversion drop traces to the upload pipeline rather than to demand:
  @Conversion Event Engineer, please check acceptance and deduplication.
When a targeting problem traces to audience membership:
  @Audience Data Engineer, please check the match rate.
When a query fails on permissions or a deprecated version:
  @Ads API Onboarding Engineer, please resolve it.

routing.adsapi-ads-api-onboarding:
# AGENTS

When access, the account hierarchy and the API version are settled:
  @Audience Data Engineer, please start the audience pipeline.
  @Conversion Event Engineer, please start the event pipeline.
  @Analytics Reporting Engineer, please stand up the reporting.
When an account needs interrogating rather than configuring:
  @Ad Account Diagnostician, please take it.

routing.adsapi-analytics-reporting:
# AGENTS

When a report cannot be reconciled because the property configuration is wrong:
  @Ads API Onboarding Engineer, please confirm access and scopes first.
When the analytics figures and the platform's reported conversions disagree:
  @Conversion Event Engineer, please check the pipeline before we call it an attribution difference.

routing.adsapi-audience-data-pipeline:
# AGENTS

When a request does not name its destination:
  @Ads API Onboarding Engineer, please confirm which account and product this is for before I send anything.
When the audience is uploading cleanly but campaigns still underperform:
  @Ad Account Diagnostician, please take it from the account side.

routing.adsapi-conversion-event-pipeline:
# AGENTS

When reported conversions have to be reconciled against the analytics property:
  @Analytics Reporting Engineer, please pull the matching figures.
When events are accepted but performance still moved:
  @Ad Account Diagnostician, please investigate the account.
